  "intro": {
    "language": "en",
    "text": "Philip Hallen Dybvig (born May 22, 1955) is an American economist. Since July 2026, he has been a university professor at Southwestern University of Finance and Economics and a visiting scholar at the Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis. He was the Boatmen's Bancshares Professor of Banking and Finance at the Olin Business School of Washington University in St. Louis from 1990 to 2026.\n\n",
    "sourceId": "wikipedia-en",
    "usage": "Research excerpt; paraphrase and cross-check before publication."
  },
